 \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}.$  Find the maximum value of\n\\[\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}),\\]where $\\mathbf{a}$ is a unit vector.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"19d818f8ecdfc25e423979565165654df309e6994d6190fc58c5abe6c8e7304c"},"seconds":46.385183811187744,"seed":99988284803150418,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to find the maximum value of \\(\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\), where \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) is a unit vector. We start by understanding the expression \\(\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\).\n\nFirst, observe that \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\) is a vector perpendicular to both \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), and \\(\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\) is the scalar triple product, which represents the volume of the parallelepiped formed by the vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\), \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), and \\(\\mathbf{c}\\).\n\nTo maximize \\(\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\), we need to maximize the magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\), since \\(\\mathbf{c}\\) is fixed. The magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\) is \\(\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\sin \\theta\\), where \\(\\theta\\) is the angle between \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\). Since \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) is a unit vector, \\(\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| = 1\\), and the maximum value of \\(\\sin \\theta\\) is 1, which occurs when \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) is perpendicular to \\(\\mathbf{b}\\).\n\nThus, the maximum value of \\(\\|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\|\\) is \\(\\|\\mathbf{b}\\|\\). We now compute \\(\\|\\mathbf{b}\\|\\):\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{b}\\| = \\sqrt{(-1)^2 + 4^2 + 6^2} = \\sqrt{1 + 16 + 36} = \\sqrt{53}.\n\\]\nTherefore, the maximum value of \\(\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\) is the magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{c}\\) times the magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), which is \\(\\|\\mathbf{c}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|\\). We now compute \\(\\|\\mathbf{c}\\|\\):\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{c}\\| = \\sqrt{2^2 + (-7)^2 + (-10)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 49 + 100} = \\sqrt{153}.\n\\]\nThus, the maximum value of \\(\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\) is:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{c}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| = \\sqrt{153} \\cdot \\sqrt{53} = \\sqrt{153 \\cdot 53} = \\sqrt{8109}.\n\\]\nTherefore, the maximum value is \\(\\boxed{\\sqrt{8109}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\sqrt{8109}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
